// TEST: Antisym Even Kernel (rejects)
// ERROR: BL4015
// THE soundness probe for compact-class inheritance. deduceOutputType's rank-0
// elementwise arm used to hand the input group's storage class to the output
// VERBATIM, for any kernel — sound only when the kernel commutes with the
// class's mirror involution. v*v does not: it is sign-EVEN, so the true result
// is SYMMETRIC (out(j,i) = f(-C(i,j)) = f(C(i,j)) = out(i,j)), while strict
// antisymmetric storage answers every mirrored read with NegateOnSwap. Before
// the check this compiled and ran, with out(0,1) = 4 and out(1,0) = -4 where
// both are +4 — a silent wrong ANSWER, not a wrong shape.
//
// The compiler refuses rather than demoting to symmetric or dense: the loop
// nest's simplex comes from the INPUT record (buildLoopLevelStructure reads
// SharedIndexTypes), so an antisymmetric input drives the STRICT simplex and
// writes C(n,2) cells. The symmetric answer needs C(n+1,2) — it has a diagonal
// this nest cannot fill. 167 shows the decompact-first spelling that works.
let A = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0]
let g = lambda(x, y) where comm(x, y) -> x - y
let C = method_for(A, A) <@> reynolds(g, Antisymmetric) |> compute
let out = method_for(C) <@> lambda(v) -> v * v |> compute
// EXPECT: typecheck failure — an even map of an antisymmetric array is
// symmetric, so it cannot inherit the strict-triangular storage.
